# Activity scene — visiting the grandparent, third time. cast.md § 3.3: "A
# moment where the grandparent asks the player something direct that nobody
# else would ask." She won't tell the player what to do.
# TODO: authenticity check

{GameState.grandparent_word} watches you put the milk away, and then watches you not sit down.
"Can I ask you something? Are you happy?"
Not how are you. Not how's the ministry. Are you happy.
- "Yes."
	[signal arg="RELIEF:1"]
	She looks at you for a while. "Good," she says. "Good. That's all I wanted to know." She reaches for your hand.
- "I don't know."
	[signal arg="RELIEF:2"]
	[signal arg="FLAG:told_grandma"]
	She nods, like that's an answer too. "That's alright. Nobody knows, half the time." She pats the couch. "Sit. You don't have to know anything in here."
